# NODX Documentation Layout {#docs-layout}

This example uses the native documentation layout. The left navigation is built from top-level headings; the right outline follows section headings.

## Authoring Model {#authoring-model}

Documentation pages remain ordinary NODX documents. The layout is selected with `theme: docs` or `layout: docs`.

### Headings Drive Navigation {#headings-drive-navigation}

Stable heading IDs create reliable sidebar links and section outlines.

### Responsive Structure {#responsive-structure}

The renderer emits a three-column shell on desktop and collapses navigation for narrower screens.

## Component Libraries {#component-libraries}

Packaged documents can carry component templates and package-local `.nods` themes.

### Local First {#local-first}

Package extensions resolve from the ZIP contents, so previews work offline and in host tools such as editors.

### Remote Resolver Contract {#remote-resolver-contract}

Remote component libraries should be fetched by the host, checked with integrity, then applied through the same package extension APIs.
